Approach 4 — Circular Linked List

Another possible implementation is a circular linked list.

Instead of:

10 → 20 → 30 → null

we can make:

10 → 20 → 30
↑           ↓
└───────────┘

Maintain a pointer to the rear.

Then:

rear.next

is the front.

This gives O(1) enqueue/dequeue.

Code
class MyCircularQueue {
        Node node = new Node(value);


        if (isEmpty()) {


            rear = node;
            rear.next = rear;


        } else {


            node.next = rear.next;
            rear.next = node;
            rear = node;
        }


        size++;


        return true;
    }


    public boolean deQueue() {


        if (isEmpty()) {
            return false;
        }


        if (size == 1) {


            rear = null;


        } else {


            // rear.next is front
            rear.next = rear.next.next;
        }


        size--;


        return true;
    }


    public int Front() {


        if (isEmpty()) {
            return -1;
        }


        return rear.next.val;
    }


    public int Rear() {


        if (isEmpty()) {
            return -1;
        }


        return rear.val;
    }


    public boolean isEmpty() {
        return size == 0;
    }


    public boolean isFull() {
        return size == capacity;
    }
}

