Why Circular Array Is Most Optimal Here

The problem is specifically:

Design Circular Queue

So the circular-array implementation directly demonstrates the intended concept.

The key trick is:

rear = (rear + 1) % data.length;

and:

front = (front + 1) % data.length;

Instead of shifting:

[10,20,30,_,_]

when 10 is removed, we simply move:

front
 ↓
[10,20,30,_,_]
    ↓
[10,20,30,_,_]

The 10 can remain physically in memory because it is no longer part of the logical queue.

